## 3. Features implemented

**Implemented:**

- One shared Qdrant collection using 3072-dimensional Gemini embeddings and cosine distance.
- Collection dimension and distance validation. Existing collections are not deleted or recreated.
- Qdrant payload indexes for `user_id`, `document_id`, `indexed`, and `chunk_index`.
- Per-chunk payloads containing user ID, document ID, chunk ID, source filename, page number, chunk index, and text.
- Stable UUIDv5 chunk point IDs, based on document ID and chunk order.
- Retry logic that replaces a document’s prior vectors instead of accumulating duplicate or stale chunks.
- An `indexed` marker: vectors are written as unindexed and become searchable only after the full upsert and database completion update.
- PostgreSQL document lifecycle updates through the existing status column.
- Authenticated `/ask` retrieval filtered to the caller’s user ID.

The existing document lifecycle and authenticated ownership routes were already present from the preceding document-management work; this phase updated how those documents are ingested into Qdrant.

